      "heading": "Finding a defect is not the problem",
      "text": "Under the Road Traffic Act 1988, using a vehicle in a dangerous state is an offence. The duty sits with the driver and the operator. The DVSA guide says drivers' defect reports must be given to a responsible person, recorded, and kept with details of any repair. Telling someone by phone is not a system."
